      "incorrect": "The match finished tie.",
      "correct": "The match ended in a tie.",
      "note": "Use **end in a tie**, with **in a**."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "He has a good tie with his boss.",
      "correct": "He has a good relationship with his boss.",
      "note": "With one person, **relationship** is more natural; **ties** is usually plural and used for families, groups, or countries."
    }
  ],
